          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#as_a_classifying_topos As a classifying topos
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of cyclic sets, being a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+category"} presheaf category
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+topos"} classifying topos
            for some
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+theory"} geometric theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abstract+circles"} abstract circles
            (
            %a{:href => "#Moerdijk96"}> Moerdijk 96
            ). A further analysis can be found in (
            %a{:href => "#CaramelloWentzlaff14"}> Caramello Wentzlaff 14
            ). Accordingly there is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-action"} infinity-action
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            of a cyclic set (see also
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Drinfeld03"} Drinfeld 03
          %h3#ModelCategoryStructure
            Model category structure and
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
          %p
            There is a
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+theory"} equivariant homotopy theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#Spalinski95"}> Spalinski 95
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Blumberg04"} Blumberg 04
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+category"} cyclic category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+cohomology"} cyclic cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+space"}> cyclic space
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclotomic+spectrum"} cyclotomic spectrum
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skew-simplicial+set"}> skew-simplicial set
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+set"} symmetric set
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
          %h2#references References
          %p The original definition:
          %ul
            %li#Connes83
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alain+Connes"}> Alain Connes
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Cohomologie cyclique et foncteurs
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Ext
                            %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ext^n
                %strong 296
                (1983), Série I, 953-958
                %a{:href => "https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=777584"} MR777584
                %a{:href => "https://zbmath.org/?q=an:0534.18009"} Zbl0534.18009
                (
                %a{:href => "https://alainconnes.org/wp-content/uploads/n83.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Connes_CohomologieCyclique.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Cartier"}> Pierre Cartier
                , Section 1.6 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homologie cyclique : rapport sur des travaux récents de Connes, Karoubi, Loday, Quillen…
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/?id=SB_1983-1984__26__123_0"} numdam:SB_1983-1984__26__123_0
          %p
            Textbook account (in the generality of
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+spaces"} cyclic spaces
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Louis+Loday"}> Jean-Louis Loday
                ,
                %em
                  Cyclic Spaces and
                  = succeed "-Equivariant" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
                (
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-662-21739-9_7"}> doi:10.1007/978-3-662-21739-9_7
                )
              %p
                Chapter 7 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cyclic Homology
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 301
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-662-21739-9"} doi:10.1007/978-3-662-21739-9
            %li#Loday11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Louis+Loday"}> Jean-Louis Loday
                , Section 3 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Free loop space and homology
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Free Loop Spaces in Geometry and Topology
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 24
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1110.0405"} arXiv:1110.0405
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/emsilmtp-24"} ISBN:978-3-03719-153-8
          %p Exposition:
          %ul
            %li#Malkiewich15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cary+Malkiewich"}> Cary Malkiewich
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em A visual introduction to cyclic sets and cyclotomic spectra
              %em Young Topologists Meeting
              Lausanne, Switzerland (2015) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://people.math.binghamton.edu/malkiewich/ytm_2015.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Malkiewich-Cyclic.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion of the relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alain+Connes"}> Alain Connes
                , Caterina Consani,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cyclic structures and the topos of simplicial sets
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1309.0394"} 1309.0394
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Julie+Bergner"}> Julia E. Bergner
                , Walker H. Stern,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cyclic Segal Spaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.11945"} abstract
          %p
            The identification of the category of cyclic sets as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+topos"} classifying topos
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abstract+circles"} abstract circles
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Moerdijk96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"}> Ieke Moerdijk
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cyclic sets as a classifying topos
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MoerdijkCyclic.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#CaramelloWentzlaff14
              %p
                Olivia Caramello, Nicholas Wentzlaff,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cyclic theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1406.5479"} arXiv:1406.5479
          %p
            The resulting circle-action on the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            of) cyclic sets is also discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Drinfeld03
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Drinfeld"}> Vladimir Drinfeld
              ,
              %em On the notion of geometric realization
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0304064"}> arXiv:0304064
              )
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            of cyclic sets and its relation to
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+theory"} equivariant homotopy theory
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Spalinski95
              %p
                J. Spalinski,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Strong homotopy theory of cyclic sets
            %li#Blumberg04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Blumberg"}> Andrew Blumberg
                ,
                %em
                  A discrete model of
                  = succeed "-homotopy" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0411183"}> arXiv:math/0411183
                )
